%S A185897 1,2,9,64,574,5919,67205,820258,10602848,143710500,2028137178,
%T A185897 29649220223,447247229447,6940546801219,110540089124381,
%U A185897 1803424905623166,30092225956558590,512900050694933194,8920102424129086072,158152113262621615772,2856378228939048222912,52517755925150547407706
%N A185897 G.f. A(x) satisfies: A(x - A(x)^2) = x/(1-x).
%C A185897 Conjecture: for n > 1, a(n) is odd when n = 3*2^k through 4*2^k - 1 for k >= 0. - _Paul D. Hanna_, Oct 05 2025
%C A185897 The conjecture is true (see Preil link). Proof sketch: the defining equation determines A(x) uniquely over the integers, so it suffices to solve it mod 2. Over GF(2) put L(y) = Sum_{k>=0} y^(2^k), so that L(y)^2 + L(y) = y. Then B(x) = L(x + x^3)/(1 + x) satisfies B(x + B(x)^2) = x/(1 + x), because with u = x + B^2 one has u = L(x+x^3)/(1+x)^2 and L(u + u^3) = x(1+u)/(1+x), verified by the Artin-Schreier identity. Hence A(x) == L(x + x^3)/(1 + x) (mod 2), whose coefficients are 1 exactly for n = 1 and 3*2^k <= n <= 4*2^k - 1. - _Dovid Preil_, Oct 16 2026
%H A185897 Paul D. Hanna, <a href="/A185897/b185897.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..400</a>
%H A185897 Dovid Preil, <a href="https://github.com/dpreil-ydlp/open-problems/blob/master/math/A185897/PROOF.md">Proof of the parity conjecture</a>, with independent review and computational verification to 400 terms, Oct 2026.
%F A185897 G.f. A(x) = Sum_{n>=1} a(n)*x^n and the related series G(x) (the g.f. of A389476) satisfy the following formulas.
%F A185897 (1) A(x - A(x)^2) = x/(1-x).
%F A185897 (2) A(x) = G(x)/(1 - G(x)) where G(x - A(x)^2) = x.
%F A185897 (3) G(x) = x + A(G(x))^2 where G(x) = Series_Reversion(x - A(x)^2).
%F A185897 From _Dovid Preil_, Oct 16 2026: (Start)
%F A185897 A(x) == (x + x^2 + x^3 + x^4 + x^6 + x^8 + x^12 + x^16 + x^24 + ...)/(1 + x) (mod 2), where the numerator is Sum_{k>=0} (x^(2^k) + x^(3*2^k)).
%F A185897 a(n) mod 2 = parity of #{m <= n : m = 2^k or m = 3*2^k for some k >= 0}. (End)
%e A185897 G.f.: A(x) = x + 2*x^2 + 9*x^3 + 64*x^4 + 574*x^5 + 5919*x^6 + 67205*x^7 + ...
%e A185897 Related expansions.
%e A185897 x - A(x)^2 = x - x^2 - 4*x^3 - 22*x^4 - 164*x^5 - 1485*x^6 - 15286*x^7 - ...
%e A185897 where A(x - A(x)^2) = x/(1-x).
%e A185897 Let G(x) be the g.f. of A389476, which begins
%e A185897 G(x) = x + x^2 + 6*x^3 + 47*x^4 + 442*x^5 + 4691*x^6 + 54330*x^7 + 672992*x^8 + ... + A389476(n)*x^n + ...
%e A185897 then A(x) = G(x)/(1 - G(x)) and G(x - A(x)^2) = x.
%o A185897 (PARI) {a(n) = my(A=x+2*x^2, B=x/(1+x+x*O(x^n))); for(i=1,n, A=serreverse(B - subst(A,x,B)^2)); polcoef(A,n)}
%o A185897 for(n=1,25,print1(a(n),", "))
%Y A185897 Cf. A389476, A213591.
%K A185897 nonn,changed
%O A185897 1,2
